---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/demo/"]}>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">Watch the Otto demo</span>
      </nav>
      <section class="tool-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">An interactive workflow guide</div>
        <h1>Walk through a visit with Otto.</h1>
        <p>
          Explore the workflow described on Otto’s public site. This guide
          illustrates the steps; it does not record audio, create clinical
          notes, or connect to a patient chart.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section
        class="demo-video-section"
        id="watch"
        aria-labelledby="watch-heading"
      >
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Product walkthrough</span>
            <h2 id="watch-heading">Watch Otto in action.</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="micro">Recorded July 2026 · Added October 16, 2026</span>
        </div>
        <video
          class="demo-video"
          controls
          playsinline
          preload="metadata"
          poster="/assets/demo-poster.svg"
          aria-label="Otto product demo, recorded July 2026"
        >
          <source src="/media/otto-demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          <p>
            Your browser cannot play this video.{" "}
            <a href="/media/otto-demo.mp4">Download the Otto demo</a>.
          </p>
        </video>
        <p class="micro">
          Explore the workflow steps below after watching. This recording shows
          the product as it appeared in July 2026.
        </p>
        <a class="button" href="/waitlist/">
          Join the Otto waitlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </section>
      <div class="step-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Visit workflow">
        <button
          role="tab"
          id="tab-0"
          aria-controls="step-0"
          aria-selected="true"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          1. Prepare
        </button>
        <button
          role="tab"
          id="tab-1"
          aria-controls="step-1"
          aria-selected="false"
          tabindex="-1"
        >
          2. Draft
        </button>
        <button
          role="tab"
          id="tab-2"
          aria-controls="step-2"
          aria-selected="false"
          tabindex="-1"
        >
          3. Confirm
        </button>
        <button
          role="tab"
          id="tab-3"
          aria-controls="step-3"
          aria-selected="false"
          tabindex="-1"
        >
          4. Close
        </button>
      </div>
      <section
        class="workflow-panel"
        role="tabpanel"
        id="step-0"
        aria-labelledby="tab-0"
      >
        <span class="tag">Step 1 of 4</span>
        <h2>Visit preparation</h2>
        <p>
          Review the patient record and last-session context. Bring your own
          clinical judgment to the summary before starting the next visit.
        </p>
        <span class="status-chip">Patient context → Visit preparation</span>
      </section>
      <section
        class="workflow-panel"
        role="tabpanel"
        id="step-1"
        aria-labelledby="tab-1"
        hidden
      >
        <span class="tag">Step 2 of 4</span>
        <h2>Draft and review the note</h2>
        <p>
          With the appropriate consent, capture session audio and generate a
          draft. Check the SOAP or DAP structure, correct the details, and sign
          the note when it reflects the encounter.
        </p>
        <span class="status-chip">
          Session audio → Draft → Clinician review → Signature
        </span>
      </section>
      <section
        class="workflow-panel"
        role="tabpanel"
        id="step-2"
        aria-labelledby="tab-2"
        hidden
      >
        <span class="tag">Step 3 of 4</span>
        <h2>Confirm proposed record updates</h2>
        <p>
          Review extracted diagnoses, treatment-plan items, and medication
          changes. Accept the items that belong in the record and dismiss those
          that do not.
        </p>
        <span class="status-chip">
          Signed note → Proposed updates → Your confirmation
        </span>
      </section>
      <section
        class="workflow-panel"
        role="tabpanel"
        id="step-3"
        aria-labelledby="tab-3"
        hidden
      >
        <span class="tag">Step 4 of 4</span>
        <h2>Review the charge and payment</h2>
        <p>
          Check the prefilled code against the service and documentation. Review
          the fee and payment details before using the collection workflow.
        </p>
        <span class="status-chip">
          Reviewed service → Charge review → Payment
        </span>
      </section>
      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>Take your questions into the product.</h2>
        <p>
          Use the official Otto sign-in page to access your account or review
          available signup options. For an evaluation, start with fictitious
          information and confirm the service terms before entering patient
          data.
        </p>
        <a class="button" href="https://otto.tebra.com/login">
          Open Otto sign-in ↗
        </a>
        <div class="tool-support">
          <a href="/security/">Security review questions ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <script is:inline src="/assets/demo.js"></script>
    </div>
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="cta">
          <div>
            <h2>Make more room for the work you love.</h2>
            <p>
              See how Otto brings notes, scheduling, telehealth, and payments
              into your practice day.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
            Join the waitlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
